 #:seon.task{:name "program-movement-is-checked-three-ways-per-form"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Each form asks whether its program moved three ways: trusted-evaluation over the loaded-identity atom, acquired-database? with loaded-program-current? over the program-identity cache (and reacquires inside evaluate), and installation-covers-program-change? after settlement. The JVM loaded-identity check is the ruled one; the branch-program check belongs once to the turn fork, never inside evaluate. Measured 2026-10-08 (HEAD ff351d2b5): in the model pass after a contracted defn acquired-database? costs 14-31 ms (about 1-2 ms otherwise), all of it acquisition-attributes (2 calls, 42 ms in the first run) re-deriving program-attributes and projection-attributes for the new projection, which program-attributes documents as about 50 ms per projection over the packaged population; the identity and basis comparisons are 0 ms. Removing it needs the derivation keyed by the schema content that changed rather than by projection."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/trusted-evaluation seon.sci.eval/acquired-database? seon.sci.eval/installation-covers-program-change? seon.sci.eval/evaluate}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/eval-path-audit-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-result-handle-is-bound-at-three-sites"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An evaluation's value is interned under its result handle by shown-result, again by `seon.turn/evaluate-sources` (commented ONE BIND SITE), and through the ::bind-result! callable seon.error carries. The print stage, which needs the handle, is the one bind."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/shown-result seon.sci.eval/bind-result! seon.turn/evaluate-sources}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/eval-path-audit-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-refused-run-leaves-its-program-in-the-context"
             :kind :function
             :intent "After a refused run the agent's SCI context still carries that run's uncommitted program and projection until the next run replaces them; bounded but a stale world between runs (probe-i, cc91a1e62)."
