             :intent "F3: defmacro inside let/when is refused as unindexed because SCI's defmacro expansion drops the form's source location (sci fns.cljc ~363-399; eval.clj ~627-673); the exact-span join the eval-path redesign relies on needs locations preserved through SCI's macro expansion (fork change)."
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/valid-clojure-corpus-probe-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-cannot-read-the-private-code-it-must-change"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(doc `seon.render.value/tree`) answers documentation-unavailable because tree is private, though every private function is contracted and is what an agent edits; source, dir and doc are not referred in an agent's user namespace ('Unable to resolve symbol: source') although help teaches them; (clojure.repl/source f) works but prints to :out and draws the :large-output finding that tells the agent to return the value instead. Doc of a public function splits its summary mid-sentence at the first line break. Give an agent doc and source of private declarations as data (the declaration's stored source and contract), referred like help's other names (repl-dogfood 2026-09-27)."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.lookup/program-documentation seon.repl/response}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "replaced-and-acquisition-ms-have-no-producer"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The evaluation keys `:seon.eval/replaced` and `:seon.eval/acquisition-ms` were produced only by `seon.sci.eval/evaluate`'s text path, which acquired the program on demand; the fold's evaluation frame never acquires, so nothing writes them. seon.turn still copies them into receipts (turn.clj evaluation facts) and seon.cluster.eval.edn declares them as attributes. Done when both attributes, their seon.config.eval and seon.turn readers and success-evaluation's handling are retired, or a fold-side producer (the run's fork acquisition) supplies them with a named consumer."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/evaluate seon.sci.eval/acquire! seon.sci.eval/fork-for-turn}
             :evidence #{"resources/seon/schemas/seon.cluster.eval.edn"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-defn-reply-prints-before-its-own-change-applies"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The defn/deftest reply is printed before its own change is applied: `seon.batch/evaluate-step` prints (batch.clj ~371) before derive-step, and the change reaches the working program only at the next form's apply-pending (batch.clj:480), so the Var render shows the state without the form's change. Shown text is stored in the settlement, so printing cannot wait. Done when the reply prints against the working program plus the form's own change; the committed assertion a-function-without-a-contract-is-admitted-and-stored in cluster/agent_test stays red until then."
             :must-read #{seon.batch/apply-pending seon.batch/evaluate-step}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/repl-audit--change.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "value-storage-walks-serializes-and-stores-every-value-up-to-eight-megabytes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "value-storage (eval.clj:3524) admits the whole printed value again with `seon.sci.admit/admit-value` under `:seon.config.eval.result/max-bytes` 8,388,608, discards the EDN it built, then re-serializes the print node with `seon.render.value/artifact-edn` and settles that copy into the blob tier, on every evaluation whose shown text was cut. Measured on default 2026-10-07 through MCP sci: (vec (range 100000)) costs 505 ms, 900 MB and 1,315,014 armed calls (`seon.print/print-number?` 600,128, node-child? 500,132, node? 100,010, `seon.sci.admit/semantic-leaf` 100,000: about 13 armed calls per element), of which show/storage is 386-400 ms, and writes 5.27 MB; a 1 MB string writes +1,083 KB; an infinite (map f (range)) is realized 157,403 elements to show 32. Our work and our stored copy grow with the value up to the 8 MB bound, per evaluation. Fix at the producer, one path: the print floor's one walk already measures the whole value; take the stored artifact (if it has a consumer) from that walk, never a second admission and a third serialization, and make the per-node predicates internal steps of the one contracted walk instead of separately armed calls. Done when (vec (range 100000)) shows in under 50 ms with under 1,000 armed calls and allocation independent of length beyond the shown prefix, and an infinite lazy seq is realized only as far as it is shown; regressions: those two cases plus a 1 MB string, asserting stored bytes."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/shown-result seon.sci.admit/admit-value seon.render.value/artifact-edn}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/waste/large-values.edn" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/waste/jfr-vec1e5-alloc.txt"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "doc-prints-contracts-expanded-with-keys-garbled"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An agent's (doc f) prints the function's contract fully expanded with map entries garbled into [[schema] [schema]] pairs (the key replaced by its schema): (doc `seon.sci.eval/install-evaluated-rows!`) costs 1,907 estimated tokens, twice the function's source, and hides which keys the input needs. doc must show the contract as declared (registry names, one level) through the value printer. Done when a regression asserts (doc install-evaluated-rows!) shows its declared :malli/schema form with its keys and is smaller than its source."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.lookup/program-doc-var}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-examples/README.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "bare-source-and-apropos-do-not-resolve-in-an-agents-repl"
             :kind :function
             :intent "In an agent's SCI context (source x) and (apropos s) are unresolved; only clojure.repl/source-fn and clojure.repl/apropos work, and (clojure.repl/source x) prints to :out with a nil value. Agents reach for the clojure.repl names first (live run 1, context-examples). Done when an agent evaluation of (source `my.task/steps`) and (apropos \"steps\") in a fresh agent world returns the source text and matching symbols as values, asserted by a regression through the agent entrance."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/build-base-ctx}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-examples/README.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/live-run/report.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "find-doc-floods-out-with-thousands-of-tokens"
             :kind :function
             :intent "clojure.repl/find-doc in an agent's REPL prints about 5,600 tokens of every matching docstring to :out, outside the value printer and its budget. Lookup tools must return values the value printer shows (matching symbols with one doc line each, dig forms for the rest), never print. Done when a regression asserts an agent's (find-doc \"task\") returns a value whose shown reply stays within the reply budget and :out is empty."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/build-base-ctx}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-examples/README.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-fresh-contexts-result-handles-have-no-regression"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Since c08e2c766 an evaluation's value is never stored: a fork without a carried agent context (a restart) binds each settled handle result/eN to a marker {`:seon.eval/unstored` :live-only, `:seon.eval/value-class` <class when recorded>} (`seon.sci.eval/bind-settled-results!`), and a refused read of the handles rides the fork as `:seon.sci.eval/unbound-results`. No test reaches either. Done when one entrance-level regression settles evaluations of a cut vector, nil and a host object through the ordinary path, checks the carried context still holds the original value by identity, forks fresh and reads each handle's marker, and checks no value blob was staged."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/bind-settled-results! seon.sci.eval/fork-for-turn seon.turn/settlement-projection}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/spec-reviews/review-batch-a-opus.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/spec-reviews/review-batch-a-review-astra-batch-a.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "live-results-are-held-for-the-contexts-lifetime"
             :kind :function
             :intent "bind-result! interns every evaluation's value in the agent context's result namespace and in its ::result-objects atom, and nothing ever releases one: on default (pid 30874, 2026-10-07, db-watch lane) root's context holds 1,311 values (every MCP jvm-mode probe of every lane), waste-rank-probe 245 including 7 collections over 10,000 elements, heap-retained-probe 215; the live heap after a full GC is 3.32 GB with 15.45M java.lang.Long (371 MB), consistent with a retained (vec (range 1e7)). Twelve finished probe agents keep their branches and contexts (nobody retired them). Values are runtime only by owner ruling, so the context is their only home; it needs a declared bound, not a store. Smallest fix: keep the newest N handles per agent (a configured dial, e.g. 64) and the values the agent's def/atoms reference; older handles bind the `:seon.eval/unstored` marker, as a fresh fork already does. Done when 1,000 jvm-mode probes of (vec (range 1e5)) leave root's live heap within the bound (measured: class histogram after GC, watch.clj :live-results-by-agent), with a regression on the retained count."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/bind-result! seon.sci.eval/fork-for-turn}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/db-watch/findings.md"}}
