             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/install-first-party-namespaces! seon.sci.eval/enter-namespace!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/interpreted-tier.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-namespace-def-that-fails-to-interpret-is-used-as-its-refusal"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A top-level `def` of a test namespace that fails to interpret installs a refusing root (`seon.sci.eval/install-refusing-root!`), and a test then uses that root as the value: \"seon.schema.datahike/malli->datahike-schema-in refused argument 0 `projection`: expected a map, got an instance of seon.sci.eval$refusing$refused\", or a fixture write \"requires a carried schema projection\" (20 interpreted-only reds, class F, e.g. `seon.db-test/a-merge-shares-the-write-fence-and-records-immutable-lineage`). Done when the failing defs are named with their causes and each interprets, or the test refuses by the def's name instead of using its refusal as data."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/install-row! seon.sci.eval/install-refusing-root!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/interpreted-tier.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-macro-reading-the-compiler-env-cannot-interpret"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A test-file macro that reads the compiler `&env` as `clojure.lang.Compiler$LocalBinding` cannot interpret, because SCI passes symbols: \"Cannot interpret seon.cluster.turn-test/with-render-context-proc: class clojure.lang.Symbol cannot be cast to class clojure.lang.Compiler$LocalBinding\"; `seon.cluster.agent-test/with-connection` fails the same way (10 interpreted-only reds after removing the Var-redefining tests, class M). Done when those macros read nothing from the compiler environment, or are functions."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/install-row!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/interpreted-tier.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-dev-namespace-test-cannot-run-interpreted-on-a-cluster"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A test of a `dev/` Babashka namespace (`seon.dev.mcp-bridge-test`, `seon.dev.docstring-test`, `seon.dev.hook-test` and others) cannot interpret on a cluster, which never loads `seon.dev.*`, so `seon.test/resolve-test` answers \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\" (25 interpreted-only reds, class D). Owner ruling 2026-10-10: interpret `dev/` (the `seon.dev.*` namespaces under `script/`) from source like any unloaded program namespace, through `seon.sci.eval/install-selected!`. Re-measured on default a740b1e26 as agent eval-fixes-3 (run 317d57b480eb): the 6 `seon.dev.docstring-test` tests pass only because the JVM happens to have loaded `seon.dev.docstring`; the 18 `seon.dev.mcp-bridge-test` tests error because `seon.dev.mcp` is not loaded; `seon.dev.publication-launch-test` errors although `seon.operator` is loaded, because it names the private `seon.operator/launch-form` and a host namespace copy exposes only public Vars. Indexing `script/` was blocked by `seon.sci.eval/a-script-namespace-contract-naming-a-local-def-crashes-publication` (fixed: the contract is kept as `:seon.fn/malformed-spec`); with \"script\" added to `seon.fn/source-roots` and `seon.test.cache/graph-roots` the check JVM (lane publication-robust, operator-check-20261010T195506) next refuses boot with \"Program indexing transaction was refused. Nothing found for entity id [:seon.ns/name user]\": script/seon/dev/settlement_probe.clj and script/seon/dev/context_corpus.clj are Babashka scripts with no `ns` form, so their defs land in `user`, which has no namespace entity. Done when these tests interpret from their source whether or not the JVM loaded their namespace."
             :must-read #{seon.test/resolve-test seon.sci.eval/source-namespace?}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/interpreted-tier.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "await-event-refuses-an-interpreted-tests-event-source"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.test-support/await-event!`, called from an interpreted test, refuses its source (\"The test event source is not a channel, latch, future, or watched reference.\"), or the wake it waits for is never observed (14 interpreted-only reds, class E, e.g. `seon.cluster.host-test/an-ordinary-message-wakes-the-idle-hosted-agent`). Done when an interpreted wake test observes its event as its compiled form does."
             :must-read #{seon.test-support/await-event!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/interpreted-tier.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "remaining-interpreted-only-test-differences"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The 2026-10-10 interpreted tier left 57 tests red only when interpreted, with no single cause yet: test.check or Malli rejecting values built in SCI (5, e.g. `seon.error-test/normalization-is-total`); instrumentation keyed by host Var (3, e.g. `seon.db-test/instrumented-wildcard-pull-keeps-unparsed-database-fields-ordinary`); test rows that did not interpret for other reasons, such as the library private Var `datahike.query/create-plan-via-ir` (3); and 46 unclassified assertion differences, listed on the evidence page. Done when each is classified to its owner or green interpreted."
             :must-read #{seon.test/resolve-test seon.sci.eval/install-row!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/interpreted-tier.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "program-identity-caches-live-outside-seon-cache"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.sci.eval/program-identity-cache` and `seon.sci.eval/refusal-recording-cache` are `clojure.core.cache` LRUs with a hardcoded threshold of 256 entries (`seon.sci.eval/program-cache-policy`), outside `seon.cache`: no byte weight, no configured dial, no `recordStats`, against the one-central-cache law. Done when both are `seon.cache` kinds keyed by commit id (identity) and by program basis and recording target (refusals), weighed at insert under the configured byte budget, and the two defonces and the policy map are deleted."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/program-identity seon.sci.eval/remember-program-identity! seon.sci.eval/record-refusals-once! seon.cache/lookup}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-script-namespace-contract-naming-a-local-def-crashes-publication"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Indexing `script/` as a program root (adding \"script\" to `seon.fn/source-roots`, to interpret `seon.dev.*` for task `seon.sci.eval/a-dev-namespace-test-cannot-run-interpreted-on-a-cluster`) made the throwaway check JVM fail boot: `seon.cluster/populate-source!` -> `seon.fn/index!` -> `seon.schema/structural-schema` threw `:malli.core/invalid-schema` for `format-findings-request-schema`, a `def` that `seon.dev.docstring/format-findings` names inside its `:malli/schema` (lane eval-fixes, 2026-10-10, operator-check-20261010T193157). One malformed authored contract refused the whole publication, where the law preserves a malformed contract as data and never arms it. `script/` holds 93 `:malli/schema` forms (73 in `seon.operator`). Done when publication preserves such a contract as data with a recorded refusal on its function and boot proceeds."
             :must-read #{seon.fn/index! seon.schema/structural-schema seon.cluster/populate-source! seon.fn/source-roots}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-interpreted-test-namespace-runs-without-its-fixtures"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An interpreted test namespace runs without its `clojure.test/use-fixtures` (class F remainder of the 2026-10-10 interpreted tier, root's go 2026-10-10). Two gaps. First, at the agent REPL (agent eval-fixes-4, default a740b1e26): `(use-fixtures :each f)` stores the fixture on the HOST namespace of the same name (its value is that namespace's metadata, `{:clojure.test/each-fixtures (f)}`), while `clojure.test/test-vars` reads `(meta (:ns (meta var)))`, the `sci.lang.Namespace`, whose metadata is nil; `(clojure.test/test-vars [#'fixture-probe-test])` ran the body alone. Second, a namespace's unnamed top-level forms (`use-fixtures`, schema registration) are not program rows, so `seon.sci.eval/install-selected!` never evaluates them. Root's design: the namespace entity holds its unnamed top-level forms (no clj-kondo var or namespace definition starts at them) as an ordered list with their byte offsets, interpreted in file order with the defs; they get no identity, and write-back keeps them through the namespace. A first proof attempt (lane eval-fixes, check runs f3fe095070c5 and 7887ca74bc25) evaluated `use-fixtures` then a deftest through `seon.test-support/evaluate` on a forked context: the deftest's evaluation answered \"Program row could not be installed; correct the reported acquisition evidence.\" instead of its Var, both in `seon.sci.eval-test` and in a fresh `ns`; that refusal is the first thing to read. Evaluating `use-fixtures` in a host-loaded namespace also adds the fixture to the compiled namespace's metadata. Done when an interpreted deftest runs inside its namespace's fixtures."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/install-selected! seon.sci.eval/run-tests seon.test.runner/run-vars! seon.fn/index!}}]
